{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-24) — re-scope: the \"detect sustained outage\" premise is REJECTED\n\nThe premise of this ticket is faulty: **we cannot reliably detect a sustained outage.** At the\n`LLMUnavailableError` catch point a transient blip and a multi-hour outage are indistinguishable,\nand any heuristic trigger (first-outage / after-N / after-a-window) would either fire too eagerly\n(regressing ADR 0040's retry posture) or be arbitrary. Therefore **there is NO distinct\n\"sustained outage\" handling** and **ADR 0040 is NOT amended**. This resolves design question #1\n(sustained-detection trigger) by removing it.\n\n### The behavior we DO want (this is the spec)\n\n1. **Retryable errors follow the normal retry pattern** — bounded retries with **backoff**, and on\n   *terminal* exhaustion a **clear operator message** (an actionable \"completion verifier could not\n   execute — retry\" surface, the exit-11 \"transient — retry\" posture from ADR 0040). No verdict is\n   fabricated from a run that could not execute.\n2. **Certified PASS is unreachable if the completion verifier could not execute.** A run that never\n   completed its criteria can never yield a certifiable PASS — unchanged, correct, keep it.\n3. **A partial, operator-actionable BLOCK is surfaced as a BLOCK.** When the criterion bank holds a\n   partial result that is itself operator-actionable (a real, banked BLOCK/FAIL on an evaluated\n   criterion), finalize a **BLOCK verdict from the bank** so the operator gets the available\n   feedback — rather than dying verdict-less. This BLOCK is `certifiable=False` and does **not**\n   auto-close the ticket (operator decision required). An **empty** bank has nothing actionable to\n   surface, so it stays on the retry path (#1).\n\n### What this changes from the escalation\n\n- Removes AC framing around detecting/handling \"sustained\" outages.\n- Keeps the `assemble_deterministic_verdict` finalizer as the mechanism, but the **trigger is \"the\n  bank already holds an operator-actionable BLOCK,\"** not \"the outage is sustained.\"\n- The close-boundary contract (design question #2) stands: a `certifiable=False` BLOCK **refuses to\n  close** and is operator-actionable; PASS-without-execution remains impossible.\n\n### Next\n\nImplementable now. Retitling to drop the \"sustained outage\" framing. RED->GREEN with a held-out\noracle + defect-seeded mutation per the original AC4. No ADR change required."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787592827445316001,"uuid":"56afa0a2-6fd3-4289-ae15-9f155e4b70a3"}